3. Question 1 – Sensor Monitoring System
3.1 Objective
The objective of Question 1 was to develop a C program for a simplified water-quality monitoring system.
The program receives:
- Temperature in degrees Celsius.
- Turbidity in NTU.
It then calculates a water-quality index and classifies the water as Good, Warning, or Critical.
3.2 Water-Quality Calculation
The water-quality index is calculated using:
Index = 100 - (TemperatureDeviation + TurbidityPenalty)

Where:
TemperatureDeviation = |Temperature - 25|
TurbidityPenalty = Turbidity / 2

The classification is:
Index	Status
80 or above	Good
60–79.99	Warning
Below 60	Critical


3.3 Implementation
The program uses a separate function to calculate or classify part of the water-quality result. This demonstrates the use of user-defined functions instead of placing all logic inside main().
