5.5 Advantage of Recursion
One advantage of recursion is that it can provide a simple and clear solution for problems that can naturally be divided into smaller versions of the same problem.
5.6 Limitation of Recursion
A limitation is that recursion uses additional memory for function calls. For very large inputs, excessive recursion can result in high memory usage or stack overflow.
6. Question 4 – Arduino Smart Parking System
6.1 Objective
Question 4 involved designing and simulating a smart parking-space monitoring system using an Arduino Uno.
The system detects whether a vehicle is within a predefined distance of the ultrasonic sensor and provides a visual and audio indication of the parking status.
The required data flow is:
Ultrasonic Sensor
        ↓
    Arduino Uno
        ↓
Decision / Processing
     ↙       ↘
   LEDs     Buzzer

6.2 Components Used
The system uses:
- Arduino Uno
- Ultrasonic distance sensor
- Green LED
- Red LED
- Buzzer
- Resistors
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires
6.3 Component Roles
Ultrasonic Sensor
The ultrasonic sensor measures the distance between the sensor and an object, such as a vehicle.
Arduino Uno
The Arduino acts as the controller. It receives the distance measurement, processes it, and decides whether the parking space is available or occupied.
Green LED
The green LED indicates that the parking space is available.
Red LED
The red LED indicates that the parking space is occupied.
Buzzer
The buzzer provides an audio alert when a vehicle is detected within the defined occupancy threshold.
6.4 Decision / Processing
A distance threshold is used to determine the parking status.
For example:
If distance > threshold:
    Green LED ON
    Red LED OFF
    Buzzer OFF

If distance <= threshold:
    Green LED OFF
    Red LED ON
    Buzzer ON

This decision-making process is performed by the Arduino after receiving the measurement from the ultrasonic sensor.
